🚀 Day 9 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 74 – Search a 2D Matrix.

This problem strengthened my understanding of Binary Search by applying it in two stages—first to identify the correct row and then to search for the target element within that row.

💡 Approach: Two-Level Binary Search

Instead of scanning the entire matrix, I first performed Binary Search on the rows to find the only row that could contain the target. Once the correct row was identified, I applied Binary Search again within that row to locate the target efficiently.

This approach leverages the sorted properties of the matrix and achieves an optimized O(log m + log n) time complexity.

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Applying Binary Search on a 2D Matrix
✅ Breaking a problem into smaller search spaces
✅ Performing Binary Search in multiple stages
✅ Utilizing matrix properties for optimization
✅ Achieving efficient searching with O(log m + log n) time complexity

